      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017, Copyright the Authors Journal compilation © 2017, The American Geriatrics Society.",
        "AbstractText": "New information on infectious diseases in older adults has become available in the past 20 years. In this review, in-depth discussions on the general problem of geriatric infectious diseases (epidemiology, pathogenesis, age-related host defenses, clinical manifestations, diagnostic approach); diagnosis and management of bacterial pneumonia, urinary tract infection, and Clostridium difficile infection; and the unique challenges of diagnosing and managing infections in a long-term care setting are presented."
      },
